    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Equation 5.5b is Wright's formula (1937), which holds provided the genotypic fitnesses are constant and frequency independent (not themselves functions of allele frequencies, which can be formally stated as $ \\partial W_{ij}/\\partial p_k = 0 $ for all $ i, j $, and $ k $. Normal derivatives are used in Equation 5.5b as there is just a single variable, the allele frequency $ p $.",
      "source_page": 116,
      "source_pages": [
